I think option 2 would be nice. I would probably start by adding `bool String::equalsn_span(const Span<char32_t> &p_lhs , const Span<char32_t> &p_rhs)`. This should be a relatively simple loop.

And then `begins_withn_span` could be pretty trivial in the header:
```c++
static bool begins_withn_span(const Span<char32_t> &p_string, const Span<char32_t> &p_span) {
    return p_string.size() >= p_span.size() && equalsn_span(Span(p_string.ptr(), p_span.size()), p_span);
}
```
